            },
            "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/TokTok/qTox/commits/5e09f325d31e649831e7a0b25676e4c5d0097d6d/comments",
            "commit": {
                "author": {
                    "date": "2025-04-04T21:04:31Z",
                    "email": "nurupo.contributions@gmail.com",
                    "name": "Maxim Biro"
                },
                "comment_count": 0,
                "committer": {
                    "date": "2025-04-04T21:41:38Z",
                    "email": "nurupo.contributions@gmail.com",
                    "name": "Maxim Biro"
                },
                "message": "fix: Call the correct QString::args() overload in Qt 6.9\n\nQt 6.9.0 redesigned the QString::args() overloads, making sure that\ncharacter-like types always output a character instead of a number. This\nresults in the compile failure, as there is no longer an overload for\nQString::arg(const char32_t&, int, int, QChar). To get the old behavior\nof printing the number and to fix the compile failure, we must cast the\ncharacter to an integral type, so that the integral overload is called.\n\nSee the commit message of:\nhttps://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/563ed822f867c6c3040956017d4ca7f3795f172c\n\nFixes TokTok/qTox#585",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "4c5333f868d81a431990b8b42098ace43e8a4bcb",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/TokTok/qTox/git/trees/4c5333f868d81a431990b8b42098ace43e8a4bcb"
                },
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/TokTok/qTox/git/commits/5e09f325d31e649831e7a0b25676e4c5d0097d6d",
                "verification": {
                    "payload": "tree 4c5333f868d81a431990b8b42098ace43e8a4bcb\nparent 95eaad2f45cf0763bd31e156fafb16e6b74be1cb\nauthor Maxim Biro <nurupo.contributions@gmail.com> 1743800671 -0400\ncommitter Maxim Biro <nurupo.contributions@gmail.com> 1743802898 -0400\n\nfix: Call the correct QString::args() overload in Qt 6.9\n\nQt 6.9.0 redesigned the QString::args() overloads, making sure that\ncharacter-like types always output a character instead of a number. This\nresults in the compile failure, as there is no longer an overload for\nQString::arg(const char32_t&, int, int, QChar). To get the old behavior\nof printing the number and to fix the compile failure, we must cast the\ncharacter to an integral type, so that the integral overload is called.\n\nSee the commit message of:\nhttps://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/563ed822f867c6c3040956017d4ca7f3795f172c\n\nFixes TokTok/qTox#585\n",
                    "reason": "valid",
